messages:  [['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nAnne is big. Anne is smart. Bob is cold. Gary is big. Gary is furry. Harry is not cold. Harry is green. All young people are cold. If someone is smart then they are young. If someone is furry then they are green. Green people are white. If someone is green and cold then they are white. If Harry is green and Harry is young then Harry is furry. Green people are furry. All cold people are furry. If Gary is green then Gary is furry.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? Anne is not white.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "Anne is not white" is true, false, or unknown based on the given information, let\'s analyze the context step by step:.\n\n1.**Anne is big.** (No direct information about color.).\n2.**Anne is smart.** (No direct information about color.).\n3.**Bob is cold.** (No direct information about color.).\n4.**Gary is big.** (No direct information about color.).\n5.**Gary is furry.** (No direct information about color.).\n6.**Harry is not cold.** (No direct information about color.).\n7.**Harry is green.** (No direct information about color.).\n8.**All young people are cold.** (No direct information about color.).\n9.**If someone is smart then they are young.** (No direct information about color.).\n10.**If someone is furry then they are green.** (No direct information about color.).\n11.**Green people are white.** (No direct information about color.).\n12.If someone is not green and warm then they are not white.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
