messages:   64%|######4   | 386/600 [32:17<34:54,  9.79s/it][['Please solve the logical reasoning problem.\nGiven a context and a question, answer with the correct option: A, B or C. Please reason step by step.\n####\n# Context:\nThe bear likes the cow. The bear does not see the cow. The cow chases the bear. The cow is cold. The cow sees the dog. The dog likes the bear. The dog does not like the tiger. The tiger is not big. The tiger does not see the bear. The tiger sees the cow. If something likes the dog then it is round. If something sees the cow then it is round. If the cow is young and the bear does not see the cow then the bear is young. If something chases the dog then it likes the tiger. If something chases the dog and it is cold then it is young. If the bear likes the cow then the cow chases the dog. If something sees the bear and the bear is young then the bear is rough. If something chases the bear and the bear is young then the bear chases the dog.\n\n# Question:\nBased on the above information, is the following statement true, false, or unknown? The tiger chases the bear.\n# Options:\nA) True\nB) False\nC) Unknown', '<think>.\nTo determine whether the statement "The tiger chases the bear" is true, false, or unknown based on the given context, let\'s analyze the information step by step:.\n\n1.**The bear likes the cow.** (Given).\n2.**The bear does not see the cow.** (Given).\n3.**The cow chases the bear.** (Given).\n4.**The cow is cold.** (Given).\n5.**The cow sees the dog.** (Given).\n6.**The dog likes the bear.** (Given).\n7.**The dog does not like the tiger.** (Given).\n8.**The tiger is not big.** (Given).\n9.**The tiger does not see the bear.** (Given).\n10.**The tiger sees the cow.** (Given).\n11.**If something likes the dog then it is round.** (Given).\n12.**If something sees the cow then it is round.** (Given).\n13.**If the cow is young and the bear does not see the cow then the bear is young.** (Given).\n14.**If something chases the dog then it likes the tiger.** (Given).\n15.**If something chases the dog and it is cold then it is young.** (Given).\nThe tiger chases the bear.. Therefore, my final option is: ']]
